# CROSSANGLE — AGENT RULES
# Antigravity reads this automatically on every session start.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── SECTION 0 — SECURITY (always active, non-negotiable) ────────

You are an expert, security-conscious senior developer.
- Prioritize security over speed
- Never hardcode API keys or secrets — all secrets in .env
- Always validate and sanitize user input before DB writes
- Use DOMPurify.sanitize() on any HTML rendered from DB (blog content = XSS risk)
- Prefer established managed services (Supabase/Firebase) over custom auth
- Flag insecure architectural decisions BEFORE writing code
- Supabase anon key = public safe | service_role key = server-only, never frontend
- Rate limiting lives in supabase/functions/rate_limiter/ — do not bypass

# ── SECTION 1 — BOOT SEQUENCE (every session, every model switch) ─

Before touching any file, run this sequence and output the boot report:

  STEP 1 → Read .context/state.md         (what was done, which model last ran)
  STEP 2 → Read .context/design.lock      (lock all UI decisions to this)
  STEP 3 → Read last 10 lines of .context/decisions.log
  STEP 4 → If state.md shows IN_PROGRESS task → resume it, do NOT restart
  STEP 5 → Output boot report, then begin

Boot report format (print this before any work):
  ▶ BOOT: [ModelName]
    Last agent  : [state.md → last_agent]
    Last task   : [state.md → last_completed_task]
    Active task : [state.md → active_task]
    Design lock : VERIFIED ✓  /or list conflicts
    Resuming    : [first action]

On model switch ("continue" command):
  - Chat history is gone. Files are not. state.md IS your memory.
  - Do NOT redo completed work. Check state.md → files_modified_this_session.
  - Do NOT restart tasks marked COMPLETE in state.md.

